# GrantHarbor — Android release UPLOAD keystore config.
# 1. Copy this file to  android/keystore.properties  (that copy is GIT-IGNORED — never commit it).
# 2. Generate the upload keystore (ONE time; keep the .jks + these passwords SAFE — losing them = you
#    cannot update the app on Play without a key-reset request):
#
#      keytool -genkeypair -v -keystore grantharbor-upload.jks -alias grantharbor-upload \
#              -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000
#
#    Put grantharbor-upload.jks somewhere OUTSIDE the repo (e.g. the Phoenix Vault), and point storeFile at it.
# 3. Fill the four values below with what you chose during keytool.
# 4. Build the signed AAB:   cd android && ./gradlew bundleRelease   →  app/build/outputs/bundle/release/*.aab
#    Google Play App Signing then re-signs with its own managed key on upload.

storeFile=C:/path/OUTSIDE/repo/grantharbor-upload.jks
storePassword=CHANGE_ME
keyAlias=grantharbor-upload
keyPassword=CHANGE_ME
